# Privacy Policy — Birthday Countdown

_Last updated: November 22, 2026_

Birthday Countdown reminds you of birthdays and important dates, helps you plan the gift and gets the
message ready. It works without an account or a server: **what you add stays on your phone**.
This policy explains what the app uses, why, and what happens in the free plan, which shows ads.

## 1. What stays on your phone

Dates, people, gift ideas, budgets, notes, messages, photos you pick for cards and backgrounds, and
your settings are stored only on the device. We have no server, create no account and never
receive a copy of this data.

## 2. Permissions

Each permission is requested only when you use the feature, and the app keeps working if you deny
it.

| Permission | Why |
|---|---|
| Contacts | Import birthdays and call the person. Read on the device. |
| Calendar | Import events that repeat every year. Read on the device. |
| Notifications and alarms | Remind you of dates at the time you choose. |
| Photos | Add photos to cards and date backgrounds. |
| Files | Save and open backups and lists you export or receive. |

## 3. Backup and sharing

Backups, lists and cards are files that **you** export and send wherever you like (email, cloud,
messages). From then on, the policy of the service you chose applies.

## 4. Ads (free plan)

The free plan shows ads from **Google AdMob**. To serve and measure ads, Google may collect the
device advertising ID, the IP address (and the approximate location derived from it), device and
system information, and interactions with ads.

- Where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland), the app
  asks for your consent first, through Google's consent platform, and you can change it later.
- On iPhone, the system asks whether the app may track you across apps; without permission, the
  advertising ID is not used.
- With **Premium** there are no ads and the ads SDK is not started.

How Google uses this data: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>.

## 5. Purchases

Subscriptions and the lifetime purchase are processed by **Google Play** or the **App Store**. We
never receive your payment details; the app only asks the store whether Premium is active.

## 6. Internet

The app uses the internet only for ads (free plan) and the store (purchases and restore). Links
you open, such as a gift shop, open outside the app.

## 7. Children

The app is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect children's data.

## 8. Retention and deletion

Data stays on the phone until you delete it in **Settings > Backup and data** or uninstall the
app. Backups you exported stay where you saved them. Since we keep none of your data, there is
nothing to delete on our side; requests about ad data can be made to Google in your account or
device ad settings.

## 9. Your rights

You have the rights granted by the LGPD (Brazil), the GDPR (Europe) and similar laws. Contact us at
the email below with any question or request.

## 10. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top is updated and relevant changes are announced in the
app.

